-- title:
--   Original HJB signed BV stopped budgets yield exact real perpetual cash and terminal L1
-- statement:
--   From actual original bounded-variation HJB conditions and the exact signed closed finite-horizon dividend-cash plus surviving postpayment terminal budget, derive automatically the real initial candidate nonnegativity and the time-zero/pre-ruin jump secant. The accepted real Stieltjes L1 bridge provides terminal L1 at every positive horizon, finite perpetual dividendValue, exact ENNReal.ofReal of the expected true signed perpetual Stieltjes cash, and the real expected cash upper bound.

